# This is a model of a sand wedge buried in shales. The C & G preprint
# has a discussion of this model. Here's some things you can do

# The demos here use bigendian data. Su takes this directly if compiled with SUXDR on (I recommend this)
# if your SU install is not SUXDR and little endian, insert suswapbytes at suitable pipes (|) below

# See the seismic
cat near-stack.su |   suxwigb

# See the underlying mean prior model
delivery -v 3 -p -m prior_traces.su ModelDescription.xml ; 
deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su -l   | suximage blockinterp=1

(or easy inbuilt graphics)
deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su -l -G 

# See samples from the prior
delivery -v 3 -PD -N 100   -IS -m prior_traces.su ModelDescription.xml ; \
deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su -l   | suximage blockinterp=1

(or easy inbuilt graphics)
deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su -l -G 

# To make Random walk sampler (-RWS) realisations
delivery -PD -v 3 -RWS  -N 100 -m prior_traces.su ModelDescription.xml

# to see them:
deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su -l   | suximage blockinterp=1
OR
deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su -l -G 

# to see the p50 thickness of the wedge
deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su --quantile thickness 2 50

# to plot it
deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su --quantile thickness 2 50 | awk '{print $NF}' | graph -TX -a

# To see some sphaghetti plots of posterior synthetics on top of truth case (see the script...)
make_spaghetti_plots.sh -PD -RWS -N 100

# or the easy inbuilt way...
deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su --trace-filter 'tracl=8' -S 1.7 2.1 R_near wavelet.su near-stack.su -G



Forcing pinchouts
_________________

There are cases when you need to force a pinchout. The inverter
detects such forcing by feeding it an isopach (thickness) constraint
of 0 thickness with 0 uncertainty (sigma_thickness=0).  In this case,
the layer bottom-time is synchronised with the top time in the model,
and all internal properties are omitted from the model (if possible)
to reduce computation time. See ModelDescriptionForcingPinchout.xml
for an example. The test perl script make_wedge_model.pl can generate
the required traces in the flavours you may require.  Beware: later
analysis of the internal properties of these suppressed layers may not
contain meaningful numbers (no sampling is performed on them, as they
cannot contribute to the seismic response and thus the likelihood).
